WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.660
Between The Wild Hunt, The White Flame, and
why everyone seems to want a piece of Ciri,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.100
there are a lot of head-scratching moments
in the first five episodes of Season 3 of

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.700
"The Witcher."

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.969
Francesca lost her newborn daughter in Season
2, and that set off a series of catastrophic

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:19.350
events for not only the Elves but for everyone
who has come into contact with them.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.020
After a tentative alliance with Nilfgaard
orchestrated by Fringilla, the Elves were

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:28.352
lulled into a false sense of security only
for devastation to ensue when her child was killed.

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:32.360
This led Francesca to lash out and kill several
Nilfgaardian children.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.570
The reveal that the Nilfgaardian king, Ciri's
father, was the culprit in this horror makes

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.090
it all the more upsetting.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:42.190
The grief over her child is overwhelming,
and it makes sense that Francesca's judgment

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.630
is completely compromised.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:47.840
But no one else seems to be making particularly
good decisions either.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.350
Francesca's only purpose now is revenge, but
that's all the more reason why her support

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.870
system should be stepping up and giving her
time to properly grieve.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.579
We know that the Elves have had serious problems
with their leaders in the past, so it's kind

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:02.219
of surprising that there aren't better safeguards
in place for taking care of her.

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:06.680
Yet, the only attempts made to bring Francesca
back to her senses have been either gentle

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.060
coaxing or outright betrayal.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.470
Both of these strategies have made the situation
drastically worse.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.009
As it is, she's a mother who has lost not
just her child, but the hope for a better

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:20.400
future for her people, making her the most
dangerous kind of leader.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.190
Maybe it isn't so much that Elf history is
confusing, just that we don't know all that

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.380
much about it, and everything we learn leaves
us with more questions.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:31.390
For instance, "Blood Origin" did the handy
work of explaining a bit of context around

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.650
the Conjunction of the Spheres, an event that
saw worlds merge and delivered an influx of

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.759
humans and monsters to the world.

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:41.700
Even still, we get the feeling that the four-episode
spin-off only scratched the surface.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.939
We met some major players and saw the beginning
of the decline of the Elven empire, but that's

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:49.799
a far way away from actually explaining the
full history of the Elves.

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:53.700
When Geralt is captured by Elves in the first
season, they're hanging on by a thread after

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.500
centuries of anti-Elf aggression and attacks.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.900
In Season 3, we hear a bit more about Elven
history as Yennefer and Geralt tell Ciri the

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.579
tale of an ancient hero.

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:08.143
Even that legend seems entirely open to interpretation
as Ciri offers counterpoints to Yennefer's narrative.

00:02:08.143 --> 00:02:12.200
When it comes to the Elves, we're getting
a lot of exposition in a very condensed format,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.800
but if you have questions about what the Elves
have been up to since, well, forever, we're

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.470
right there with you.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:21.060
Considering that they didn't particularly
want to be bothered by Geralt or his friends

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.140
to begin with, Codringer and Fenn's untimely
demise at the hands of Reince came as a bit

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.140
of a shock.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.900
When Reince arrives at the library, it's not
clear what his true motives are for torching

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.510
the place and its occupants.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:36.430
The two researchers gave Geralt only a sparse
amount of intel during his visit, but it costs

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.760
them their lives, and we can't help but feel
it was a bit of an escalation.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.170
While it shows us that Reince is willing to
resort to abject cruelty to accomplish his

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.209
goals, we kind of already knew that.

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:50.150
We can't help but feel that these two were
of way more use alive than dead.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.450
"Please, not the cat."

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.040
"Tell me everything."

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.980
All of our confusion around this one may be
rooted in our love for the lovably curmudgeonly

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.040
Codringher and Fenn, their cat, and their
stellar book collection, but their deaths

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.480
still feel like a bit of a waste.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.310
Yennefer taking Ciri to Aretuza makes a lot
of sense.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:10.120
It's clearly a decision she struggles with,
as does Geralt, but they agree together to

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.650
split up for the good of the Princess.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.739
Yennefer takes her to train with the best
mages on the planet while Geralt goes after

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:19.540
Reince who continues to work in service to
a mysterious benefactor.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.680
This is a choice they all struggle with, particularly
Yennefer, who knows the Brotherhood's hypocrisy

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.129
and balks at the idea of taking Ciri to them
despite her faith in their ability to keep

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:29.129
her safe.

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:32.950
Though Yennefer explains her own history to
Ciri, she doesn't prepare Geralt's adopted

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.689
daughter for how hard the mages are on their
novices.

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:39.450
She also doesn't fully explain the strange
political climate that made it such a struggle

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.700
for her to train there.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.440
When Ciri first meets some of Yennefer's fellow
mages, she's immediately treated like a servant.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.680
She bristles at this, and though Yennefer
explains to her that this is how you play

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:52.930
politics in the world of magic, it's not enough
to convince Ciri, who flees on horseback.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:57.370
Though Ciri's brash flight from the town is
in character for her, it definitely exposes

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.420
a lack of understanding about the severity
of her situation.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.730
Yennefer's feelings toward Tissaia, the Brotherhood,
and Aretuza are complex.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.769
She views Tissaia both as a mother figure
and friend while still acknowledging her more

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:11.460
severe personality traits.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.590
Life at Aretuza is what gave her power, but
she suffered at the hands of her teachers

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:16.959
and fellow students.

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:21.109
Finally, the Brotherhood has long served as
a thorn in her side due to its hubris and

00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:22.790
unwillingness to change.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.880
But she admires their power and sees herself
as one of them, even if she occasionally chafes

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.139
at the idea.

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:32.130
Tissaia's fondness and pride in Yennefer are
clear, but she continues to keep secrets from

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.130
her pupil.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.430
This is certain to cause more harm to their
relationship.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.530
Meanwhile, the Brotherhood watched Yennefer
almost single-handedly end the Battle of Sodden

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:44.060
Hill at the end of Season 1 only to more or
less put her on trial in Season 2.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:48.250
In Season 3, they're universally annoyed by
her presence but most of the mages ultimately

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.310
see the benefits of her plea to a more united
Brotherhood.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.221
By the end of Episode 5, it seems that she's
been invited back into the fold, but this

00:04:55.221 --> 00:04:59.580
is a pretty tempestuous bunch of people, so
we'll have to wait and see.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.001
This is one where we can rest assured that
we'll find out more about it soon, but that

00:05:03.001 --> 00:05:06.800
doesn't change the fact that we still have
pretty much no clue what's going on with Ciri's

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.940
dad, the White Flame of Nilfgaard.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.910
Perhaps the biggest twist of the second season
was the reveal that he was alive at all, with

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.380
Ciri believing that he and her mother perished
at sea many years before.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.470
More shocking, he's the Emperor of Nilfgaard,
meaning that he's responsible for the damage

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.460
we've seen his invading army cause to the
Northern territories.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.800
In the novels, the White Flame is fascinated
with his daughter's elder blood.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.100
Her lineage inspires him to make choices that
are some of the most controversial plot points

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.100
of the book.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.789
While the Netflix series has stayed relatively
true to the source material, it made a few

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:40.472
major deviations last season that clued us
in that there would be more changes on the way.

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:44.600
At present, all we know of Emperor Emhyr is
his glorified tale of taking back his kingdom

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.900
with the power of his sword, but he has a
tendency of being an unreliable narrator,

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.610
so we have to take his claims with a grain
of salt.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:55.730
The build-up for the Wild Hunt has been extreme,
with "Blood Origin" diving into the distant

00:05:55.730 --> 00:06:00.470
past in no small part to introduce us to the
"leader" of this mystical group of wraiths,

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.860
Eredin Bréacc Glas.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.720
The captain of the Xin'trea military makes
several bad moves in a very short period of

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.410
time during the lead-in to the Conjunction
of the Spheres, and it costs him.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.580
First, he plans a coup with Balor then sides
with Merwyn in hopes of securing a better

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.800
future for himself and his lover, Brian.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:19.630
He is ultimately banished with several of
his men to an alternate dimension.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:23.420
While we haven't seen much in the way of his
transformation to the leader of the Wild Hunt,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.669
we can guess the story isn't a particularly
cheery one.

00:06:26.669 --> 00:06:30.099
Though this season has given us glimpses of
the awesome power of the Hunt, and we know

00:06:30.099 --> 00:06:34.037
that their pursuit of Ciri will continue,
we're still not sure what their ultimate goal is.

00:06:34.037 --> 00:06:37.889
It's hinted that Ciri's power could act as
a key to unlock the barrier between realms,

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:40.090
but perhaps they want to induct Ciri into
their group.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:43.340
Either way, we're still very much at the beginning
of their story.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:49.440
"Child of the Elder Blood, starry-eyed daughter
of chaos, join our hunt."

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.620
When we first met Vilgefortz he was manipulating
Yennefer to return to Aretuza to help him

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.949
avoid being drafted into service by the king
of Nilfgaard.

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:01.340
After that, we saw him slay a fellow mage
during the Battle of Sodden Hill.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.430
This created significant doubt about where
his loyalties lie.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:09.240
While Tissaia sees the good in him, even that
has become fairly questionable at times, particularly

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.610
when he lashed out at her during Season 2.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.240
Having taken leadership of the Brotherhood,
Vilgefortz seems calm through the first few

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.669
episodes of Season 3.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.780
He even charms Yennefer who has good reason
not to trust him.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:24.220
Using their shared love for Tissaia, he wins
Yennefer over, but to what end is still unclear.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.260
Though there are plenty of theories swirling
around him as of the fifth episode, and there

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.240
might be a major blow-up on the horizon.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.340
With Stregobor imprisoned for hiding a book
that he denies having taken, we suspect that

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:37.870
this could have easily been planted in his
room by Vilgefortz.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.360
Cahir has been a mysterious character from
the start.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.659
He lead the invasion of Cintra and attempted
to kidnap Ciri.

00:07:43.659 --> 00:07:48.500
He continues his pursuit of Ciri and in his
search massacres a group of Cintran refugees.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:53.139
He continues his rampage by enlisting a doppler
to kill Ciri's childhood mentor Mousesack

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.270
and take his form.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.539
The doppler tricks her into trusting him but
traumatizes her by leveraging her only true

00:07:58.539 --> 00:07:59.800
friend against her.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:03.599
He later kills an entire tavern of people
just to make sure none of the people inside

00:08:03.599 --> 00:08:04.599
are the doppler.

00:08:04.599 --> 00:08:08.379
Without a doubt, Cahir is one of the most
terrifying characters in the series due to

00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:10.900
his unsettling dedication to The White Flame.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.860
In Season 2, he and Yennefer are forced to
flee together after she refuses to take his

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.660
life on behalf of the Brotherhood.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.490
This sets off a chain of events that sees
him returning to Nilfgaard and allying himself

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:22.220
with the equally ruthless Fringilla.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.599
When she murders several generals for treachery
but leaves Cahir alive, it becomes clear that

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:30.530
these two have some kind of connection, but
is it just their commitment to The White Flame?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:34.550
We have seen time and again that Cahir will
do anything for the king of Nilfgaard, but

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:38.070
will discovering that Fringilla is still alive
despite the White Flamed claiming she has

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.580
died change any of that?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.017
For someone who has appeared in so many episodes,
we still don't know much about what drives Cahir.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.230
So far, we know very little of Philippa, making
her a confusing character.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:52.720
We met her in Season 2 as an owl working in
tandem with Dijkstra, but as for what her

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:57.070
specific motivations are beyond a wild grab
for power, we're still pretty clueless.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:01.620
We've seen her involved in S&amp;M with Dijkstra
and engaging in an affair with one of Vizimir's

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.540
staff, and we know she's orchestrated more
than one brutal murder, but we still don't

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:06.540
know why.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.120
One fascinating tidbit that has been dropped
in the third season is that she and Tissaia

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.350
had a falling out.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:15.250
When Yennefer asks Tissaia what happened,
the mage dismisses what happened as two friends

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.400
simply growing apart.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.190
"There's nothing to understand.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.870
The friendship just ran its course."

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.490
Yet, Philippa seems to have plenty more to
say on the subject, leaving us to wonder what

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.399
exactly went down between these two powerful
mages.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:32.120
And Philippa's mystery goes even deeper with
her connection to Aretuza and her unique mastery

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:34.450
over shapeshifting still mostly unexplained.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:38.779
At this point, these plot threads could go
in just about any direction, so we're on the

00:09:38.779 --> 00:09:40.189
edge of our seats with Philippa.

